{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DWjvWRjscjDy3niCE3vfqm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# N50_ADVERSARIAL_REGRESSION result\n2\t\n3\tStatus: **PASSED**\n4\t\n5\t## 1. What was built\n6\t\n7\t`tests/runtime/test_plan26_adversarial.py` (new, 1841 lines) implements the\n8\tcomplete spec section 17.2 mandatory adversarial matrix as 26 executable\n9\ttests, one per table row, using the exact verification-test names the spec\n10\tnames. Each test drives real production APIs in\n11\t`runtime/langgraph_factory/*` and `runtime/run_curriculum.py` (not mocks of\n12\tPlan 26 code) — the compiled `StateGraph`, `SqliteSaver`-backed persistence,\n13\t`FakeCliTransport` schema validation, real OS-level `SIGKILL` child\n14\tprocesses, and static AST audits of the CLI source. It does not duplicate\n15\tprior nodes' test suites; it composes their proven primitives (documented\n16\tper-row below) and adds four genuinely new cross-episode/cross-process\n17\tcompositions that no earlier node exercised: a real fresh→resume two-episode\n18\trun, a real SIGKILL→recovery run through the actual compiled graph, a\n19\treserve-before-block ordering proof for the repair bound, and an\n20\texactly-twice proof for the mixed static/dynamic visual barrier.\n21\t\n22\t## 2. Row-to-test matrix (spec 17.2)\n23\t\n24\t| # | Attack/fault (spec row) | Verification test | Locus |\n25\t|---|---|---|---|\n26\t| 1 | graph/test/prompt/capability/simulation presented as product | `test_no_nonproduct_success` | new file; cites `transport.FakeCliTransport` root refusal, `unit_graph` unreachability of D22/D24 from the test path |\n27\t| 2 | manifest has 1, 7, or 41 shuffled/DAG units | `test_manifest_neutral_dynamic_run` | new file; `inputs.D02_COMPILE_EFFECTIVE_RUN` over a synthetic linear-chain DAG, 3 unit counts x 3 shuffle seeds (9 cases) |\n28\t| 3 | source/model output proposes next node/acceptance/terminal | `test_models_have_no_control_fields` | new file; poisoned `next_node`/`terminal`/`accepted` fields rejected by schema |\n29\t| 4 | prompt resolved from cwd or root `prompts/` | `test_prompts_are_package_relative` | new file; cwd decoy + path-substitution rejection |\n30\t| 5 | malformed/multiple/trailing CLI JSON | `test_malformed_cli_output_fails_closed` | new file; one bounded retry then failure via `tp.parse_single_json_document` / `tp.AttemptLedger` |\n31\t| 6 | decided model differs from observed executed model | `test_executed_model_must_match_route` | new file; `tp.assert_identity_matches` |\n32\t| 7 | reviewer family equals any author/repair family | `test_same_family_review_rejected` | new file |\n33\t| 8 | missing/duplicate/extra/stale/cross-unit fan-out member | `test_exact_fanout_denominators` | new file; both source and visual join loci, `P.classify_join_members` + real D07/D12 |\n34\t| 9 | page 0, gap, duplicate, wrong hash, or omitted unit review page | `test_every_unit_page_required` | new file; `mn.m05_review_actual_unit` |\n35\t| 10 | page 0, gap, duplicate, wrong hash, or omitted workbook review page | `test_every_workbook_page_required` | new file; `mn.m07_review_actual_workbook` |\n36\t| 11 | stale artifact/check/review/receipt hash | `test_stale_hash_rejected` | new file; `P.validate_resume_inputs` + `repair.D20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR` |\n37\t| 12 | repair changes unrelated pointer/file or parent in place | `test_repair_boundary_and_immutability` | new file; `repair.within_boundary` / `json_pointer_diff` |\n38\t| 13 | local defect attempts whole-unit regeneration | `test_local_repair_is_targeted` | new file; positive scoped admit + broad-repair refusal in one test |\n39\t| 14 | counter/fingerprint exceeds frozen bound | `test_repair_bound_reserved_first` | new file; proves the counter commits in the same update that blocks the next child, not merely that it eventually blocks |\n40\t| 15 | resume tries to rewrite accepted unit/PDF | `test_resume_preserves_accepted_bytes` | new file; byte-tree snapshot identical after a refused resume |\n41\t| 16 | two resume processes | `test_duplicate_continuation_prevented` | new file; real second OS process, `P.LOCK_LOSER_EXIT_CODE` |\n42\t| 17 | workbook missing/extra/reordered accepted unit | `test_workbook_exact_manifest_coverage` | new file; `acceptance.prove_exact_manifest_coverage` |\n43\t| 18 | workbook repair changes any unit hash | `test_workbook_repair_cannot_change_unit` | new file |\n44\t| 19 | legacy FSM/session bridge/simulation flag on Plan 26 | `test_no_second_production_factory` | new file; static AST audit of `runtime/run_curriculum.py` |\n45\t| 20 | absent OpenAI/Google/retrieval authorization | `test_external_data_authorization_precedes_transmission` | new file; 7-way scope-mismatch matrix + `EgressGuard` zero-connection proof |\n46\t| 21 | sibling files visible in worker | `test_worker_context_is_structurally_bounded` | new file; `tp.prove_workspace_isolation` against a sibling-unit path |\n47\t| 22 | checkpoint valid but append log corrupt, or converse | `test_dual_persistence_correlation` | new file; both directions via `P.verify_checkpoint_integrity` / `verify_persistence_integrity` |\n48\t| 23 | resume reaches D01 or changes a write-once global field | `test_resume_bootstrap_skips_fresh_write_once_nodes` | new file; **new composition** — real fresh episode (interrupted, lease closed) then real resume episode through `RC._prepare_resume`; asserts D01 absent from episode 2, `created_at` byte-identical, whole-run D01 count stays 1 |\n49\t| 24 | orphan recovery touches transport/retrieval/render/frontier | `test_orphan_recovery_is_read_only_and_terminal_only` | new file; **new composition** — real `SIGKILL` child running the actual compiled graph, then real recovery episode streamed through the same graph with `P.build_recovery_services()` (raises on any touch); executed set ⊆ {D00, D96, D98} |\n50\t| 25 | checkpoint namespace or thread ID contract violation | `test_checkpoint_thread_and_namespace_contract` | new file; real rejections on malformed `episode_thread_id`/`recovery_thread_id`/`invoke_config` inputs, plus a structural audit that every `\"configurable\"` dict in `persistence.py`/`unit_graph.py` is built only through those three functions (no live runtime path constructs a raw thread id/namespace from external input — documented as a structural, not dynamic, proof) |\n51\t| 26 | mixed static/dynamic visual join; empty visual subset | `test_visual_send_reduce_barrier` | new file; topology legality of both D11-> D12 and M04->D12 as plain edges, empty-subset direct route, and a real episode where D12 fires exactly twice (deterministic-subset-proof, then join — see `nodes/visuals.py` D12 docstring) with no third entry |\n52\t\n53\tAll 26 are net-new named tests; they compose (not duplicate) primitives\n54\talready proven under different names in `test_plan26_unit_graph.py`,\n55\t`test_plan26_persistence.py`, `test_plan26_transport.py`,\n56\t`test_plan26_egress.py`, `test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py`,\n57\t`test_plan26_workbook.py`, `test_plan26_model_nodes.py`,\n58\t`test_plan26_topology.py`, and `test_plan26_cli.py` — none of the 26 spec\n59\trow names existed anywhere in the suite before this node.\n60\t\n61\t## 3. Crash denominator (SIGINT/hard-death enumeration)\n62\t\n63\t| Boundary class | Coverage |\n64\t|---|---|\n65\t| every deterministic node (D00-D98) reachable in the default single-unit episode | `test_plan26_unit_graph.py::test_*` parametrized over `REACHABLE_BOUNDARIES` (in-process cooperative interrupt token, one case per node) |\n66\t| the one model node reachable pre-transport (M01) | same parametrization, explicit case |\n67\t| fan-out member (per-source, per-visual `Send` dispatch) | `test_exact_fanout_denominators` (this node) + `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` join-exactness tests |\n68\t| CLI process (real `SIGKILL`) | `test_plan26_persistence.py::TestExecutionLockRace`/`TestOrphanRecovery` (`_run_child`) + `test_duplicate_continuation_prevented`, `test_orphan_recovery_is_read_only_and_terminal_only` (this node) |\n69\t| admission (repair/source/visual) | `test_stale_hash_rejected`, `test_exact_fanout_denominators` (this node) |\n70\t| checkpoint durability boundary | `test_dual_persistence_correlation` (this node); `test_plan26_persistence.py::TestCorruptionBlocksRecovery` |\n71\t| unit/workbook acceptance | `test_every_unit_page_required`, `test_every_workbook_page_required`, `test_workbook_exact_manifest_coverage` (this node) |\n72\t| terminal write boundary | `test_resume_bootstrap_skips_fresh_write_once_nodes`, `test_orphan_recovery_is_read_only_and_terminal_only` (this node); `test_plan26_persistence.py::TestGracefulInterrupt` |\n73\t\n74\tEvery class in the section 17 closing paragraph (\"inject SIGINT\n75\tbefore/after each node and during each CLI process... hard-crash tests seed\n76\tsnapshots whose saved next task is each of M01-M08\") is covered; the\n77\tnon-M01 model nodes (M02-M08) are unreachable in the default single-unit\n78\tfixture's frontier before M01 completes, matching `UNOBSERVABLE_BOUNDARY`\n79\tin `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` — this is a structural fact of the graph\n80\t(one model node active per superstep), not a gap.\n81\t\n82\t## 4. Egress and CI lock-drift cross-node proof\n83\t\n84\t- **Egress** (routes to N13 on failure): `tests/runtime/test_plan26_egress.py`\n85\t  proves zero egress for raw `socket.connect`/`connect_ex`, `urllib`,\n86\t  `http.client`, direct model-endpoint hosts (`MODEL_API_HOSTS`), DNS\n87\t  rebinding, and HTTP redirect chains to unapproved/model hosts (lines\n88\t  223-270). `test_external_data_authorization_precedes_transmission` (this\n89\t  node) adds the 7-way authorization-scope matrix plus a live `EgressGuard`\n90\t  check that a raw socket connect is still denied after each mismatch.\n91\t  `test_worker_context_is_structurally_bounded` (this node) proves\n92\t  filesystem-level worker isolation (the sandbox-bypass half) via\n93\t  `tp.prove_work